  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The Peshitta root spelled רפא means slacken or let go, answering to Hebrew רפה. It is distinct from healing. The Arabic use for repairing cloth supports the repair sense in 1 Kings 18:30. The shorter names Rapha and Raphu permit a connection with healing, although their stories offer no explanation."
